      "kind": "standard gauge",
      "note": "The main lines through Verdun in 1916, all built before 1914: Paris–Verdun by Récicourt and Regret, Verdun–Sedan along the Meuse's left bank by Charny, Marre and Cumières, Verdun–Étain by Tavannes and Eix, and Verdun–Saint-Mihiel up the Meuse by Dugny. Each was matched by eye with the railway printed on the 1916 sheets (cartes 22 and 24, 1:20 000), and IGN's present course (BD TOPO, Licence Ouverte) kept for its precision; the high-speed line, built in 2007, left out. South of Verdun, beyond the 1:20 000 sheets, checked only against the 1:80 000 sheet of 8 July.",
